            <ArticleTitle>[Study of immunoregulation of dendritic cells in allergic rhinitis].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>49-51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To investigate the immunoregulation of dendritic cells in allergic rhinitis.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHOD" NlmCategory="METHODS">Adopting the cell culture and the enzyme linked immunosorbant assay to examine the patients' Th1/Th2 in the blood. Observing that how is the DC's function in immunoregulation of allergic rhinitis.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULT" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The concentration of the IFN-gamma advanced obviously in post-stimulatory supernatant liquid after using the mature DC.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The mature dendritic cells can polarize naive T-cells into Th1 effector cells, and are recognized as having a central role in the establishment of T-cell memory and peripheral immune tolerance. DC could be exploited as targets for therapy in asthma and allergic rhinitis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
